Chrisjan,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on quarries, =
farms and remote sites; we don't sell packages.

Salt pans spread over a large area: pumps, sluices, security and the
people out on the pans all need to be reachable, and the office rarely
sees problems until someone drives out. A small owned network across the
pans puts monitoring and cameras where the work is.

I'd like to run a desk study on Swartkops Sea Salt from terrain and public
infrastructure data first: where a backbone can run across the pans and
how a reliable uplink gets onto it. It tells you what is feasible before
anyone spends money.

If that's useful, the next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you
have, what fails, what it costs you, and what an owned network would look
like. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and the report is yours
either way. The one-page proposal is attached; the short version is here:
www.cttx.co.za/assessment

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

